;; Verified public-register citations for the legal entity archived by this repository.
;;
;; Every row is checked live by tools/verify_citations.cljs:
;;   * GET :cite/url must answer HTTP 2xx
;;   * :cite/expect-substring must appear in the response body
;;
;; A URL that cannot be fetched, or whose body no longer carries the claim, is a
;; DRIFT and fails the gate. Nothing is recorded here that was not retrieved.
;;
;; THREE independent authorities are cited, not one:
;;   * GLEIF, the global LEI system
;;   * the United States, via the SEC's EDGAR submissions API (Intercontinental
;;     Exchange, Inc. is a domestic large accelerated filer, ticker ICE on the
;;     NYSE -- an exchange it owns -- CIK 0001571949)
;;   * the issuer itself, at its own published website www.ice.com -- the
;;     terms page this repository archives (80-data/public/tos.journal.edn
;;     archives https://www.ice.com/terms-of-use, the same URL the issuer-*
;;     rows cite)
;;
;; WHY NO DELAWARE STATE REGISTER IS CITED DIRECTLY. GLEIF names RA000602 -- the
;; Division of Corporations, Department of State, Delaware -- as BOTH the
;; register of record and the validation authority for this entity (rows
;; gleif-registered-at and gleif-validated-at), and the registeredAs 5298907 is
;; the Delaware corporate file number. Delaware publishes no per-entity GET URL:
;; the ICIS entity search (icis.corp.delaware.gov) answered 200 to this gate on
;; 2026-08-22, but only with its search form -- per-entity lookups run behind
;; POST/session flows and certified extracts are paid. What the catalog does
;; instead is corroborate the Delaware claims through independent authorities
;; that do answer on stable URLs: GLEIF says US-DE and legal form XTIQ, the ELF
;; code for a Delaware Corporation (rows gleif-jurisdiction, gleif-legal-form,
;; resolved by the gleif-elf-* definition rows) -> the SEC prints
;; stateOfIncorporation DE (row sec-state-incorp) -> the issuer's own terms
;; print 'a Delaware corporation' in the sentence naming the owner of the
;; Website (row issuer-owner-delaware). GLEIF records the file number 5298907
;; twice (registeredAs and validatedAs) and once more inside the OpenCorporates
;; id us_de\/5298907 (row gleif-ocid). The SEC and GLEIF never consulted each
;; other.
;;
;; THE NYSE IS VISIBLE FROM ALL THREE AUTHORITIES WITHOUT ANY OF THEM SAYING
;; 'owns'. GLEIF maps this entity to MIC XNYS -- the Market Identifier Code of
;; the New York Stock Exchange (row gleif-mic) -- and one of only THREE direct
;; children GLEIF records for it is the 'Revised Retirement Plan for Eligible
;; Employees of The New York Stock Exchange and Subsidiary Companies' (row
;; gleif-child-nyse-plan-name). The SEC records the listing exchange as NYSE
;; (row sec-exchange): the company lists on the exchange it operates. And the
;; issuer's own terms define the Website as 'www.ice.com, www.nyse.com,
;; www.intercontinentalexchange.com' in one breath (row issuer-website-family).
;; Three URL families, one relationship, no shared source.
;;
;; FOUR HONEST WRINKLES, SO A READER DOES NOT MISREAD THEM AS DRIFT:
;;   1. GLEIF's legal address is C/O UNITED AGENT GROUP INC., 1521 Concord
;;      Pike, Suite 201, Wilmington DE 19803 -- a registered-agent address,
;;      though a different agent than the Corporation Trust Center the Nasdaq
;;      sibling catalog (549300L8X1Q78ERXFD06) records. The operating
;;      headquarters is 5660 New Northside Drive, Atlanta GA 30328, and HERE
;;      GLEIF AND THE SEC AGREE TO THE STREET: GLEIF prints '5660 New
;;      Northside Drive' / '3rd Floor' / 'Atlanta' (rows gleif-hq-address,
;;      gleif-hq-city) while the SEC prints '5660 NEW NORTHSIDE DRIVE,' (with
;;      a trailing comma) / 'THIRD FLOOR' / 'ATLANTA' (rows sec-street,
;;      sec-street2, sec-city). Same fact, per-source spellings; each row
;;      matches its own source's bytes.
;;   2. The SEC submissions record carries "lei":null (row sec-lei-null): the
;;      SEC does NOT corroborate the LEI string itself. The GLEIF<->SEC join in
;;      this catalog rests on legal name + Delaware incorporation + the shared
;;      Atlanta street address + ticker (rows sec-name, sec-state-incorp,
;;      sec-street, sec-ticker), not a shared identifier.
;;   3. The SEC record prints "ein":"000000000" -- an all-zeros placeholder
;;      (row sec-ein-zeros). It is recorded because it is checked and true of
;;      the source; it identifies and corroborates nothing. The Nasdaq sibling
;;      cites a real EIN; this registrant's EDGAR record simply carries none.
;;   4. GLEIF prints the legal name upper-case (INTERCONTINENTAL EXCHANGE,
;;      INC.); the SEC prints 'Intercontinental Exchange, Inc.'. Case
;;      conventions per source, not two names.
;;
;; ONE STRUCTURAL FACT WORTH READING TWICE: the entity on this record was
;; created 2013-03-06 (row gleif-creation-date), and the SEC knew this same
;; CIK as 'IntercontinentalExchange Group, Inc.' from 2013-03-20 until
;; 2014-05-29 (row sec-former-name). The record is the holding company built
;; in 2013 for the NYSE Euronext acquisition -- not the 2000 Atlanta startup
;; whose name it now bears. The LEI followed on 2013-12-10 (row
;; gleif-initial-registration), while the SEC still carried the Group name.
;; Today the LEI is managed by Bloomberg Finance L.P., marketing name
;; 'Bloomberg' (rows gleif-managing-lou, gleif-lou-*) -- an external LOU,
;; where the Nasdaq sibling's LEI is managed by its own consolidated
;; subsidiary. The catalog cites what GLEIF answers today and claims nothing
;; about earlier managing LOUs.
;;
;; WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT CITED. GLEIF's nextRenewalDate and lastUpdateDate
;; move by construction; a row on either would go red on schedule while saying
;; nothing about the entity. The GLEIF ISIN mapping for this serial note
;; issuer moves by construction too; no per-ISIN row and no count row is
;; wanted. The issuer's page title '<title>Terms of Use</title>' names no
;; company, so it is cited as :attribute, not :identity. The children-count
;; row goes red when GLEIF adds or removes a relationship; that is correct
;; DRIFT, not a false alarm.
;;
;; :cite/row-kind is the honest part of this catalog and should be read before
;; the claims:
;;
;;   :identity   the substring names this entity, its identifiers, or a specific
;;               related legal entity (the CIK, the BIC, the MIC, the file
;;               number, the OpenCorporates id, the S&P id, the named direct
;;               children, the former name). Point the URL at a different
;;               company and the row fails.
;;   :attribute  the substring is TRUE OF THIS ENTITY BUT NOT ONLY OF IT (status
;;               ACTIVE, jurisdiction US-DE, SIC 6200, fiscal year 1231, the
;;               generic page title). Such a row can survive a swap to a
;;               similar company. It is recorded because it is checked and
;;               true, not because it identifies.
;;   :definition the row resolves a code used by another row (RA000602, ELF
;;               XTIQ, the managing LOU). It says the named register, legal
;;               form or LEI issuer exists; it says nothing about
;;               Intercontinental Exchange, Inc. except through the rows that
;;               reference it.
;;
;; Of the entries below, 22 are :identity, 33 are :attribute and 11 are
;; :definition. A reader who treats all 66 as identifying would overstate what
;; this catalog proves -- which is the error this field exists to prevent.
;;
;; Substrings are taken from the RAW response body and were each checked against
;; the fetched bytes before this file was written (2026-08-22, GLEIF golden copy
;; of 2026-08-21). GLEIF escapes URL slashes in its JSON (us_de\/5298907,
;; C\/O UNITED AGENT GROUP INC., https:\/\/corp.delaware.gov\/); the ocid,
;; address, ra-website and lou-website rows match that raw escaped form
;; deliberately.
